{"question_id":"pthe-height-of-any-point-p-above-the-surface-of-earth-is-e-jee-main-physics-motion-wle1ijful47zvdmm","qKey":"pthe-height-of-any-point-p-above-the-surface-of-earth-is-e-jee-main-physics-motion-wle1ijful47zvdmm","permalink":"pthe-height-of-any-point-p-above-the-surface-of-earth-is-e-jee-main-physics-motion-wle1ijful47zvdmm","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2022 (Online) 25th June Morning Shift","year":2022,"subject":"physics","chapter":"gravitation","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"<p>The height of any point P above the surface of earth is equal to diameter of earth. The value of acceleration due to gravity at point P will be : (Given g = acceleration due to gravity at the surface of earth).</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"g/2"},{"identifier":"B","content":"g/4"},{"identifier":"C","content":"g/3"},{"identifier":"D","content":"g/9"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>The acceleration due to gravity (g) at a distance (r) from the center of a planet is given by:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.871ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.037ex\" height=\"2.891ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -892.5 3552.5 1277.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(757.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(1813.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(786,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D440\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D440\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(555.7,-377.4) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(484,289) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1499\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>where:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>G is the gravitational constant,</li>\n<li>M is the mass of the planet,</li>\n<li>r is the distance from the center of the planet.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If the height h of a point P above the surface of the Earth is equal to the diameter of the Earth, then the distance r from the center of the Earth to the point P is 3 times the radius of the Earth. Substituting this into the equation for g gives:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.816ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16.812ex\" height=\"3.248ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1074.9 7431.1 1435.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(563.2,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2032\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-V-2032\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1085.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2141.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(2621.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0 -0.5)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(458,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" 